          %title Gauge fixing
          %h2#GaugeFixing Gauge fixing
          %p In this chapter we discuss the following topics:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#QuasiIsomorphismsBetweenBVBRSTComplexes"} Quasi-isomorphisms between local BV-BRST complexes
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %a{:href => "#GaugeFixingChainMaps"}> gauge fixing chain maps
                    ;
                %li
                  %p
                    %a{:href => "#AdjoiningAuiliaryFields"} adjoining contractible complexes of auxiliary fields
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#GaugeFixingExamples"} Example: gauge fixed electromagnetic field
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            While in the
            %a{:href => "#ReducedPhaseSpace"} previous chapter
            we had constructed the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+phase+space"} reduced phase space
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+BV-BRST+complex"} local BV-BRST complex
            (example
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalBVBRSTComplexIsDerivedCriticalLocusOfEulerLagrangeForm"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+intersection"} homotopy intersection
            with the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+histories"} field histories
            (prop.
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CovariantPhaseSpace"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+surfaces"} Cauchy surfaces
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            may still not exist (def.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CauchySurface"}
          %p
            However, with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+resolution"} homological resolution
            constituted by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
            in hand, we now have the freedom to adjust the
            = succeed "-content" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+phase+space"} reduced phase space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+cohomology"} BV-BRST cohomology
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/auxiliary+fields"} auxiliary fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+chain+complex"} contractible cochain complex
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complexes"} BV-BRST complexes
            brings the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            into a form such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of the combined
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ghost+fields"} ghost fields
            and potential further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/auxiliary+fields"} auxiliary fields
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green+hyperbolic+differential+equations"} Green hyperbolic differential equations
            after all, and thus admit a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixing
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaugeFixingLagrangianDensity"}
            below), since it is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
            which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruct
            the existence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+surfaces"} Cauchy surfaces
            (by prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NonTrivialImplicitInfinitesimalGaugeSymmetriesPbstructExistenceOfCauchySurfaces"}
            and remark
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaugeParametrizedInfinitesimalGaugeTransformation"}
          %p
            The archetypical example is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gaussian-averaged+Lorenz+gauge"} Gaussian-averaged Lorenz gauge
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} fixing
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NLGaugeFixingOfElectromagnetism"}
            below) which reveals that the gauge-invariant content of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+waves"} electromagnetic waves
            is only in their transversal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+polarization"} wave polarization
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaugeInvariantPolynomialOnShellObservablesOfFreeElectromagneticField"}
            below).
          %p
            The tool of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixing
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complexes"} BV-BRST complexes
            finally brings us in position to consider, in the following chapters, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            also of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theories"} gauge theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
            to bring the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complexes"} BV-BRST complexes
            of the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theories"} Lagrangian field theories
            into a form that admits degreewise
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+manifold"} graded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields+%28physics%29"} fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ghost+fields"} ghost fields
            and possibly further
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/auxiliary+fields"} auxiliary fields
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+differential"} BV-BRST differential
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
