          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              From
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BVDifferentialOnauxiliaryFields"} (3)
              we read off that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi aux
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mi aux
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_{aux} \coloneqq \left\{ \mathbf{L}_{aux},- \right\}
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
                  (squares to zero), and the auxiliary
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
                  satisfies its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+master+equation"} classical master equation
                  (remark
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassicalMasterEquationLocal"}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi L
                          %mi aux
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi L
                          %mi aux
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\{\mathbf{L}_{aux}, \mathbf{L}_{aux}\} = 0
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
                  of this differential is trivial:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi aux
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        H^\bullet( s_{aux} )\;=\;0
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+antibracket"} local antibracket
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-Lagrangian+density"} BV-Lagrangian density
                  with the auxiliary Lagrangian density vanishes:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi L
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mi BRST
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mi aux
                          %mo }
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\left\{
                        \- \mathbf{L} + \mathbf{L}_{BRST}
                        \\,,\,
                        \\mathbf{L}_{aux}
                        \\right\}
                        \\;=\;
                        0
            %p
              Together this implies that the sum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mi BRST
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mi aux
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\mathbf{L} + \mathbf{L}_{BRST} + \mathbf{L}_{aux}
              satisfies the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+master+equation"} classical master equation
              (remark
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassicalMasterEquationLocal"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi L
                          %mi BRST
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi L
                          %mi aux
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi L
                          %mi BRST
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi L
                          %mi aux
                        %mo )
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    \\left(
                    \- \mathbf{L} + \mathbf{L}_{BRST} + \mathbf{L}_{aux}
                    \\right)
                    \\,,\,
                    \\left(
                    \- \mathbf{L} + \mathbf{L}_{BRST} + \mathbf{L}_{aux}
                    \\right)
                    \\right\}
                    \\;=\;
                    0
            %p and hence that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi aux
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mi BRST
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mi aux
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo −
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    s + s_{aux}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    \- \mathbf{L} + \mathbf{L}_{BRST} + \mathbf{L}_{aux}
                    \\,,\,
                    \-
                    \\right\}
            %p
              is indeed a
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
              is identified with that of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mi BRST
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s = \left\{-\mathbf{L} + \mathbf{L}_{BRST},-\right\}
              under the canonical inclusion map.
          #FieldBundleBVBRST.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+formalism"} BV-BRST
                = succeed ")" do
