                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym(V^\bullet,d)
              the differential graded-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+algebra"} symmetric algebra
              that it induces (
              %a{:href => "symmetric+algebra#SymmetricAlgebraInCoChainComplexes"}> this example
              ), then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^\bullet(Sym(V,d)) = Sym(H^\bullet(V,d))
                    \\,.
            %p
              (by
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "CochainCohomologyOfSymmetricAlgebraOnCochainComplex"} this prop.
          %p In conclusion we finally obtain:
          #GaugeInvariantPolynomialOnShellObservablesOfFreeElectromagneticField.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (gauge-invariant polynomial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+cohomology"} BV-BRST cohomology
              on infinitesimal observables (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalObservablesOnInfinitesimalNeighbourhood"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalBVComplexOfVacuumElectromagnetismOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi deg
                      %mi gh
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} deg_{gh} = 0
              is the distributional polynomial algebra in the transversally polarized linear on-shell observables, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LinearObservablesOfElectromagenticFieldWavePolarization"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BRSTCohomologyOnPolynomialOnShellObservabledOfTheGaussianAveragedLorenzGaugeFixedElectromagneticField"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              By the classes of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
              of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExponentialOfLocalAntibracket"}
              and prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuasiIsomorphismAdjoiningAuxiliaryFields"}
              we may equivalently compute the cohomology if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
              with differential
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s'
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gaussian-averaged+Lorenz+gauge"} Gaussian-averaged Lorenz gauge
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} fixing
              from example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NLGaugeFixingOfElectromagnetism"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LorenzGaugeFixedEOMForVacuumElectromagnetism"} (7)
              are manifestly
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green+hyperbolic+differential+equations"} Green hyperbolic differential equations
              after this gauge fixing
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+surfaces"} Cauchy surfaces
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
              exist and hence prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NonTrivialImplicitInfinitesimalGaugeSymmetriesPbstructExistenceOfCauchySurfaces"}
              together with prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BVComplexIsHomologicalResolutionPreciselyIfNoNonTrivialImplicitGaugeSymmetres"}
              implies that the gauge fixed BV-complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi BV
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s'_{BV}
              has its cohomology concentrated in degree zero on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
              observables. Therefore prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CochainCohomologyOfBVBRSTComplexInDegreeZero"}
              (i.e. the collapsing of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
              for the BV/BRST
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicomplex"} bicomplex
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BRSTCohomologyOnPolynomialOnShellObservabledOfTheGaussianAveragedLorenzGaugeFixedElectromagneticField"}
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            This concludes our discussion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theories"} gauge theories
            obtained thereby, we may finally pass to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of field theory to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            proper, in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Quantization"} next chapter
